+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01PEspktECP1GkLfdAWgxTgR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything matches the spec exactly. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI built a reactive spreadsheet engine as a TypeScript library, organized into focused modules under `src/`:\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| `reference.ts` | Cell-ref parsing, column↔index conversion (A→AA→...), range expansion |\n| `tokenizer.ts` | Lexer for formula text (numbers, strings, cells, ops, functions) |\n| `ast.ts` | AST node type definitions |\n| `parser.ts` | Recursive-descent parser with operator precedence + reference collection |\n| `evaluator.ts` | Evaluates an AST against cell values |\n| `value.ts` | Computed value types, error model, display formatting |\n| `spreadsheet.ts` | The `Spreadsheet` class: dependency graph, reactivity, cycle detection |\n| `index.ts` | Public exports |\n\n**Key design points:**\n\n- **Reactivity** — Each cell tracks its dependencies; the engine maintains reverse edges (`dependents`). On `set`, it collects the affected subgraph and recomputes it in dependency-first topological order, so every cell sees up-to-date inputs.\n- **Cycle detection** — Before installing a formula, it walks the dependency graph forward from the new references; reaching the target means a cycle, and it throws *without mutating state* (verified by a test).\n- **Functions & ranges** — `SUM/AVERAGE/MIN/MAX/COUNT` over column/row/block ranges (numbers only; text/booleans/empties ignored), plus `IF` with all six comparison operators. `IF` only evaluates the chosen branch.\n- **Spreadsheet semantics** — Empty cells act as `0` in arithmetic; errors (`#DIV/0!`, `#VALUE!`, `#NAME?`) propagate to dependents and clear when fixed; refs are case-insensitive.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `npm test` → **62 tests pass** (3 files)\n- `npm run build` (tsc) → clean, with `.d.ts` declarations\n- `n